    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Reference implementation of <computeroutput>ai.onnx.preview::FlexAttention</computeroutput> (v1).</para>
<para>Computes <computeroutput>Y = Softmax((Q @ K^T) * scale, axis=-1) @ V</computeroutput> over rank-4 (batched, multi-head) FLOAT inputs. Supports Grouped Query Attention (GQA): when <computeroutput>q_num_heads != kv_num_heads</computeroutput> each K/V head is shared by a contiguous group of query heads, i.e. query head <computeroutput>h</computeroutput> uses K/V head <computeroutput>floor(h / (q_num_heads / kv_num_heads))</computeroutput>; <computeroutput>q_num_heads</computeroutput> must be a multiple of <computeroutput>kv_num_heads</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>The optional <computeroutput>score_mod</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>prob_mod</computeroutput> modifier subgraphs of the upstream operator are not modeled by this reference kernel — it implements the un-modified baseline that backends are expected to reproduce when neither modifier is provided.</para>
<para>Only FLOAT tensors are supported. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
